diff --git a/packs/built-in/directives/001-architectural-integrity-standard.directive.yaml b/packs/built-in/directives/001-architectural-integrity-standard.directive.yaml
index 107c9b2..7057891 100644
--- a/packs/built-in/directives/001-architectural-integrity-standard.directive.yaml
+++ b/packs/built-in/directives/001-architectural-integrity-standard.directive.yaml
@@ -10,11 +10,6 @@ scope: >
   Applies to all design proposals, implementation plans, and architectural
   decision records that introduce or modify component boundaries, module
   interfaces, or cross-cutting concerns.
-procedures:
-  - Define explicit component boundaries before implementation begins; document inputs, outputs, and dependencies for each component.
-  - Separate concerns at every layer (data, logic, presentation, infrastructure) so that changes to one concern do not propagate into others.
-  - Review proposed designs against existing boundaries to identify coupling violations before code is written.
-  - Record boundary decisions and the rationale for chosen separation in an ADR whenever the design deviates from established patterns.
 integrity_rules:
   - Components must not share mutable state across boundaries without an explicit, documented protocol.
   - Circular dependencies between components are not permitted unless the cycle is intentional, bounded, and justified in an ADR.
