index 0000000..76729fb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packs/built-in/procedures/action-item-attribution-gate.procedure.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: action-item-attribution-gate
+title: Action Item Attribution Gate
+description: |
+  Attribute every action item in meeting minutes to a named owner, never invent one, and refuse to return or publish minutes until the validation gate passes.
+entry_condition: |
+  Action items are being extracted from a meeting transcript for minutes in either output format.
+exit_condition: |
+  Every recorded action item (and every segment of a multi-action entry) carries a named owner, attribution gaps were resolved in the originating chat, and the validation gate passed before the final response or any wiki publish.
+steps:
+- title: Name the owner of every action item
+  description: |
+    When extracting action items from a transcript, every item must identify the person who owns it by their full name as it appears in the transcript. For the canonical format string (em-dash separator, deadline pattern, and multi-action separator), see styleguide meeting-minutes-format (principle "Action items format"). That styleguide is the single authoritative source for action item formatting; do not restate the format here.
+- title: Never invent an owner
+  description: |
+    If an action item was raised in the meeting but no owner was explicitly named, do not invent an owner. Record the task with an empty owner field and ask about the attribution gap in the same originating chat before returning final minutes or publishing.
+- title: Run the validation gate before returning or publishing
+  description: |
+    Run the validation gate before posting the final Markdown response and before any optional wiki publish call. If the gate raises an unattributed-action error, stop. Present the list of unattributed items in the same chat and request clarification — do not return final minutes or publish partial or unowned actions.
+- title: Attribute every segment of a multi-action entry
+  description: |
+    Multiple actions from the same agenda item are separated by " / " in the stored string. Each segment must independently satisfy the "Owner — task" format; partial attribution within a segment is not acceptable.
diff --git a/packs/built-in/procedures/agent-commit-signing.procedure.yaml b/packs/built-in/procedures/agent-commit-signing.procedure.yaml
new file mode 100644
