+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: bulk-edit-occurrence-mapping
+title: Bulk-Edit Occurrence Mapping
+description: |
+  Govern a bulk edit through an occurrence map: declare the mission occurrence-sensitive, classify every occurrence of the target term by category and action before implementation, and review against the map.
+entry_condition: |
+  A mission will rename, migrate, or replace an identifier, path, key, or term across many files.
+exit_condition: |
+  The mission is declared `change_mode: bulk_edit`, a validated occurrence_map.yaml with per-category actions and documented exceptions exists before implementation, and review evaluated changes against that map.
+steps:
+- title: Declare the mission occurrence-sensitive
+  description: |
+    Declare the mission as occurrence-sensitive by setting change_mode to bulk_edit in mission metadata.
+- title: Produce the occurrence map
+  description: |
+    Before implementation, produce an occurrence_map.yaml classifying the target term by semantic category.
+- title: Assign an action per category
+  description: |
+    For each category, assign an explicit action (rename, manual_review, do_not_change, rename_if_user_visible).
+- title: Document exceptions
+  description: |
+    Document exceptions for specific files or patterns that override category-level rules.
+- title: Gate implementation on the validated map
+  description: |
+    Implementation must not begin until the occurrence map exists and passes validation.
+- title: Review against the occurrence map
+  description: |
+    Review must reference the occurrence map as the governing artifact for evaluating changes.
