+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: change-scope-tension-resolution
+title: Change-Scope Tension Resolution
+description: |
+  Resolve the tension between smallest-viable-diff, the Boy Scout Rule, and Locality of Change on a specific change in a fixed order, and record how it was resolved.
+entry_condition: |
+  A change is being planned or reviewed and the smallest-viable-diff tactic, the Boy Scout Rule, and Locality of Change could pull in different directions.
+exit_condition: |
+  The file set and edit size were chosen first, cleanup stayed inside that file set, any extension was braked by Locality of Change, and the resolution (folded in, deferred, and why) is recorded in the task or review context.
+steps:
+- title: Start from the smallest viable diff
+  description: |
+    Start from the smallest viable diff for the stated goal (the tactic): identify the minimal file set and the minimal edit within each file before considering any further change.
+- title: Resolve conflicts in the fixed order
+  description: |
+    When smallest-viable-diff, Boy Scout Rule, and Locality of Change pull in different directions on a specific change, resolve in this order: smallest-viable-diff picks the file set and edit size first; Boy Scout Rule then governs cleanup strictly inside that file set; Locality of Change is the brake that stops either rule from growing the file set itself.
+- title: Record the resolution
+  description: |
+    Record the resolution (what was folded in, what was deferred, and why) in the task or review context rather than silently picking a side.
