+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: common-docs-page-authoring
+title: Common Docs Page Authoring
+description: |
+  Author and curate documentation inside the single Common Docs root: place pages in the styleguide's sections, keep lifecycle metadata in frontmatter, use the sanctioned keys, file ADRs by era, and retire stale documents.
+entry_condition: |
+  A documentation page or ADR is being created, moved, or updated.
+exit_condition: |
+  The page sits in the Common Docs root with frontmatter-held lifecycle metadata, uses `doc_status` and `related:` correctly (ADRs use MADR `status`), ADRs are filed under `adr/<era>/`, and stale documents are distilled and retired.
+steps:
+- title: Place pages in the single Common Docs root
+  description: |
+    Place every documentation file inside the single Common Docs root using the section structure the `common-docs` styleguide's own principle states; never create a second documentation root or a per-version shadow tree.
+- title: Keep lifecycle metadata in frontmatter
+  description: |
+    Record per-page lifecycle metadata in in-file frontmatter as the sole source of truth — the page-inventory rollup is a generated lockfile derived FROM frontmatter, never a parallel hand-maintained authority.
+- title: Use `doc_status` for the documentation lifecycle
+  description: |
+    Use the namespaced frontmatter key `doc_status` (vocabulary draft / active / deprecated / superseded / durable) for the documentation *lifecycle*; `durable` is the reserved, never-retire value for domain throughlines that are re-verified on domain change rather than aged out or retired. The bare key `status` is prohibited as a doc-lifecycle field because it collides with the work-package lane status model. Architecture Decision Records are the one sanctioned exception — ADR frontmatter uses `status` for the MADR *decision* status (Proposed / Accepted / Deprecated / Superseded), the established MADR convention.
+- title: Express cross-references with `related:`
+  description: |
+    Express cross-references with a `related:` frontmatter list of resolvable repo-relative `.md` paths; do not reintroduce the dead `citation_refs` sidecar field.
+- title: File ADRs by era
+  description: |
+    File Architecture Decision Records under `adr/<era>/` with YAML frontmatter, preserving the era-of-decision history; the living architectural design collapses into a single unversioned `architecture/` location.
+- title: Curate under the delete-stale policy
+  description: |
+    Curate under the delete-stale policy — one concern per file; DIRECTIVE_037 (Living Documentation Sync) owns the same-change documentation-update rule; stale or deprecated documents are distilled then retired rather than accumulating as a wiki.
