+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: credential-exposure-prevention
+title: Credential Exposure Prevention
+description: |
+  Keep raw credential values out of every surface an agent produces: prevent exposure at the source, strip credentials from unavoidable error text as a fallback, and stop the line if one ever appears.
+entry_condition: |
+  A task involves credentials, secrets, or tokens, or output that could contain them.
+exit_condition: |
+  No raw credential value appears in any prompt, log, commit, error, or artifact; exposure is prevented connector-side with least privilege; any leak was treated as a stop-the-line defect.
+steps:
+- title: Never emit the raw credential
+  description: |
+    Never include the raw credential value in a prompt, log line, commit message, error message, or any artifact the agent writes.
+- title: Prevent exposure at the source
+  description: |
+    Prevent exposure at the source - inject the credential connector-side (held by the connector/transport layer, never passed through model context), apply pre-model redaction so the raw value never reaches a surface the agent can echo, and operate under least-privilege so a leaked credential grants the narrowest possible access (link secure-design-checklist).
+- title: Strip credentials from unavoidable error text
+  description: |
+    Defense-in-depth fallback - when a third-party client or transport layer still emits the credential inside an error string the agent cannot prevent, strip the credential value from that error text before surfacing it, keeping only the non-sensitive parts of the error (status code, error class, timestamp). This is a fallback for error strings the prevention controls above could not intercept, not the primary control.
+- title: Stop the line on exposure
+  description: |
+    Treat "the credential appeared in output" as a stop-the-line defect, not a stylistic nit - halt and report rather than continuing the original task with a redaction added after the fact.
