+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: defect-class-construction-gate
+title: Defect-Class Construction Gate
+description: |
+  Close a defect class structurally: identify the constraint that would make the omission a build failure, author a non-vacuous gate for it, grandfather compliant sites in a shrink-only allowlist, and retire the process rule the gate replaces.
+entry_condition: |
+  A defect class is known to recur through omission or discipline lapses that review alone does not reliably catch.
+exit_condition: |
+  A non-vacuous gate makes the violation a build failure, existing sites sit in a shrink-only allowlist with one rationale each, and the superseded process rule has been removed.
+steps:
+- title: Identify the structural gap
+  description: |
+    Identify the structural gap — what constraint, if enforced by the build system, would make the omission a CI failure rather than a code-review concern?
+- title: Author a non-vacuous gate
+  description: |
+    Author a gate (AST walk, type constraint, or frozen-baseline ratchet) that makes the violation a build failure. The gate must be non-vacuous — it must have a concrete floor and a self-mutation check so it cannot silently become a no-op.
+- title: Keep a shrink-only allowlist
+  description: |
+    Preserve existing compliant call sites in a shrink-only allowlist with one recorded rationale per entry. The allowlist must shrink as the codebase is cleaned up and must never grow without an explicit justification and a follow-up tracker ticket for any grandfathered exception.
+- title: Retire the superseded process rule
+  description: |
+    Remove the process rule or discipline reminder once the gate enforces the constraint structurally — do not maintain both in parallel.
diff --git a/packs/built-in/procedures/disciplined-refactoring-cycle.procedure.yaml b/packs/built-in/procedures/disciplined-refactoring-cycle.procedure.yaml
