+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: durable-fix-investigation
+title: Durable Fix Investigation
+description: |
+  Investigate before fixing: dig for related tickets, ground the defect in current code, align with the canonical seam and ADRs, propose a structural remediation when the problem is wider than one site, and escalate recurring classes.
+entry_condition: |
+  A defect or fix request has been received and no fix has been authored yet.
+exit_condition: |
+  Related tickets, the defect site on current main, the canonical seam, and applicable ADRs are established; multi-site or structural problems are highlighted with a proposed structural remediation and a fold-vs-defer question to the operator; recurring classes are escalated.
+steps:
+- title: Investigate first, before any fix
+  description: |
+    The investigation method is mandatory and comes FIRST, before authoring any fix. Run these five steps (naturally executed as a profile-loaded investigation squad at the pre-spec / post-spec point-cuts — see procedure:adversarial-squad-deployment).
+- title: Dig for similar tickets
+  description: |
+    Dig for similar tickets. Search the WHOLE tracker (not only the current milestone) for same-surface or same-root-cause issues. Identify an existing umbrella/epic that the class belongs to, or propose one.
+- title: Ground the defect in current code
+  description: |
+    Code grounding. Trace the actual code path to the precise bypass or defect site (file:line). Confirm the bug is still real on current main — not already fixed, superseded, or an artifact of a stale base — before building on it.
+- title: Align with the canonical architecture
+  description: |
+    Architecture alignment. Map how many places implement the same concern and find the ONE canonical seam/authority all of them should route through; identify the duplication to consolidate. This is the diagnostic front-end that FEEDS DIRECTIVE_044 (single canonical authority — chase unification, not parity); it does not replace it.
+- title: Check ADRs
+  description: |
+    Check ADRs. If architecture decision records exist for the surface, read them and align the fix with the recorded decision — or explicitly amend the ADR when the durable fix supersedes it.
+- title: Propose a structural remediation
+  description: |
+    If the investigation surfaces multiple occurrences, an underdesigned seam, or a missing invariant: HIGHLIGHT them and PROPOSE a structural remediation (a shared seam, a single canonical reader, or an enforced invariant / construction gate per DIRECTIVE_043) rather than silently shipping N point-fixes. Surface the fold-vs-defer decision to the operator as a scope question BEFORE the spec, exactly like an adversarial point-cut.
+- title: Escalate recurring defect classes
+  description: |
+    When a defect class has recurred despite prior point-fixes, escalate to DIRECTIVE_040 (recurring-bug structural-intervention discipline), which mandates the five-paradigm parallel-debugging tactic — this directive is its general-purpose diagnostic front-end, DIRECTIVE_040 is the specialized escalation once recurrence is established.
diff --git a/packs/built-in/procedures/failing-test-triage.procedure.yaml b/packs/built-in/procedures/failing-test-triage.procedure.yaml
