+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: five-paradigm-structural-intervention
+title: Five-Paradigm Structural Intervention
+description: |
+  When a bug class keeps recurring, stop point-fixing: run the five debugging paradigms in parallel against one hypothesis-free bug statement, synthesize their verdicts, author one structural fix plan, and persist the evidence for future recurrences.
+entry_condition: |
+  A recurring-bug class has been detected: the same defect class has resurfaced despite earlier point-fixes.
+exit_condition: |
+  All five paradigm verdicts have been synthesized, a single structural fix plan closes the known and dormant masks, and the falsified-hypothesis catalog and divergence matrix are persisted on the parent issue.
+steps:
+- title: Dispatch the five-paradigm tactic before any further fix
+  description: |
+    When a recurring-bug class is detected, dispatch the five-paradigm parallel-debugging tactic before authoring any further fix.
+- title: Frame a single hypothesis-free bug statement
+  description: |
+    Frame a single bug statement that all five paradigms investigate independently. Do not include hypotheses in the statement.
+- title: Dispatch all five paradigms in parallel
+  description: |
+    Dispatch all five paradigms in parallel — The Falsifier, The Five-Whys Cartographer, The Bisector, The Matrix-Maker, The Stenographer. Sequential dispatch is non-compliant.
+- title: Synthesize the five verdicts
+  description: |
+    Synthesize the five verdicts. Convergence is the deliverable; divergence is signal that must be investigated, not suppressed.
+- title: Author a single structural fix plan
+  description: |
+    Author a single structural fix plan that closes all currently-known masks plus the dormant masks identified by The Matrix-Maker.
+- title: Persist the evidence on the parent issue
+  description: |
+    Persist the falsified-hypothesis catalog and divergence matrix on the parent issue so future recurrences start ahead.
+- title: Run the paradigms with the squad discipline
+  description: |
+    The general dispatch, profile-loading, and synthesis discipline for running the five paradigms as a squad lives in the adversarial-squad-deployment procedure; this directive specializes it to the five fixed debugging lenses.
diff --git a/packs/built-in/procedures/keep-change-local.procedure.yaml b/packs/built-in/procedures/keep-change-local.procedure.yaml
