+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: keep-change-local
+title: Keep a Change Local
+description: |
+  Keep a change close to the problem it solves: confine edits to the files that serve the stated goal, justify any extension beyond the touched area, keep opportunistic cleanup apart from functional work, and check the diff for scope creep before committing.
+entry_condition: |
+  A scoped change (a work package, bug fix, or task) is about to modify code, tests, or documentation.
+exit_condition: |
+  Every changed file maps to the stated goal, any extension beyond the touched area is directly connected, proportional, and documented with a rationale or tracker reference, and the diff has been reviewed for scope creep before commit.
+steps:
+- title: Limit edits to the target behaviour
+  description: |
+    Limit edits to files and modules directly related to the target behavior.
+- title: Justify any extension beyond the touched area
+  description: |
+    Before extending beyond the touched area, apply Locality of Change: the extension must be directly connected to the stated goal, proportional, and documented with a one-line rationale (or a tracker reference for anything genuinely broad).
+- title: Separate opportunistic cleanup from functional work
+  description: |
+    Separate opportunistic cleanup from functional work unless it is required for correctness.
+- title: Review the diff for scope creep before committing
+  description: |
+    Review diffs for scope creep before committing.
diff --git a/packs/built-in/procedures/land-changes-via-pull-request.procedure.yaml b/packs/built-in/procedures/land-changes-via-pull-request.procedure.yaml
