@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: land-changes-via-pull-request
+title: Land Changes via Pull Request
+description: |
+  Reach origin/main only through pull requests the operator merges, including after a consolidate and when recovering from an accidental push.
+entry_condition: |
+  Work is ready to reach origin/main, or origin/main has been pushed to directly by mistake.
+exit_condition: |
+  The change is proposed through a pull request on a PR branch (or an accidental push is reverted through a revert PR), and nothing was pushed or merged to origin/main without explicit operator instruction.
+steps:
+- title: Route every change through a pull request
+  description: |
+    All changes to origin/main must go through pull requests; never run `git push origin main` or `gh pr merge` without explicit operator instruction. The operator always merges to origin/main manually.
+- title: Open a PR after consolidate
+  description: |
+    After `spec-kitty consolidate` (which consolidates to local main only and does NOT push to origin/main), create a PR branch (`git checkout -b pr/<slug>`) and open a pull request (`gh pr create`). Do not push to origin/main directly.
+- title: Recover from an accidental push with a revert PR
+  description: |
+    Recovery if origin/main is accidentally pushed to — do NOT force-push (branch protection blocks it). Create a `revert/<slug>` branch from origin/main, commit a revert, open a PR to merge it, then open the real mission PR.
