+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: living-documentation-sync
+title: Living Documentation Sync
+description: |
+  Keep examples, acceptance checks, and documentation in step with behaviour: agree examples before planning, promote stable ones to executable checks, update every affected narrative in the same change, and retire what no longer holds.
+entry_condition: |
+  New behaviour is being planned, or existing behaviour or domain language is changing.
+exit_condition: |
+  Business-readable examples exist for new behaviour, stable examples are executable (or their non-automation is justified), every affected doc surface is updated in the same change, and stale material is removed or marked.
+steps:
+- title: Establish business-readable examples first
+  description: |
+    Establish a small set of business-readable examples before planning implementation for new behavior.
+- title: Promote stable examples to executable checks
+  description: |
+    Promote stable examples into executable acceptance checks or document why automation is not yet feasible.
+- title: Update all documentation in the same change
+  description: |
+    Update example narratives, acceptance checks, spec references, user-facing docs, code-level docs, architecture notes, and glossary entries in the same change when behavior or domain language evolves.
+- title: Remove or mark stale material
+  description: |
+    Remove or mark stale examples, doc passages, and glossary terms once they no longer describe supported behavior.
diff --git a/packs/built-in/procedures/local-tooling-selection.procedure.yaml b/packs/built-in/procedures/local-tooling-selection.procedure.yaml
