@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: local-tooling-selection
+title: Local Tooling Selection
+description: |
+  Choose fast, purpose-built local tools for each operation, record what is available, fall back only when necessary, and tell the user when a better tool is missing.
+entry_condition: |
+  An agent is about to search, inspect, or process repository content or run development operations locally.
+exit_condition: |
+  The operation used the most efficient available local tool (or a recorded fallback), tooling availability and decisions are recorded in `.kittify/memory/available_tooling.md`, and the user has been told about any missing, more efficient tool.
+steps:
+- title: Prefer purpose-built local tools
+  description: |
+    Prefer fast, purpose-built local tools over slower or noisier generic shell patterns when an equivalent local capability exists.
+- title: Record tooling availability and decisions
+  description: |
+    Record local tooling availability, session decisions, and remediation notes in `.kittify/memory/available_tooling.md`.
+- title: Use operation-appropriate tools
+  description: |
+    Use operation-appropriate tools such as ripgrep for repository search, pagers for large-file inspection, and stream-oriented archive tools for compressed content.
+- title: Favor low-overhead environment defaults
+  description: |
+    Favor environment defaults and workflow choices that reduce local overhead, including repository-safe git settings and performant Windows or WSL workflows where relevant.
+- title: Favor output-filtering tooling
+  description: |
+    Favor tooling that filters output to only the information the agent needs, reducing token consumption on common dev operations, over commands that emit unfiltered noise.
+- title: Fall back only when necessary
+  description: |
+    Fall back to less efficient tooling only when the preferred local option is unavailable or does not support the required operation safely.
+- title: Warn about missing efficient tools
+  description: |
+    When a more efficient local tool is missing, warn the user that it exists and offer to guide them through installation or setup.
diff --git a/packs/built-in/procedures/minutes-self-sufficiency-check.procedure.yaml b/packs/built-in/procedures/minutes-self-sufficiency-check.procedure.yaml
