@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: observable-contract-test-authoring
+title: Observable-Contract Test Authoring
+description: |
+  Write tests that scaffold rather than obstruct change: assert the observable contract, pin desired behaviour instead of masking defects, anchor ratchets on stable content, build fixtures through the production seam, and use production-shaped data.
+entry_condition: |
+  A test, fixture, ratchet, or allow-list is being written or changed.
+exit_condition: |
+  Assertions target the observable contract, no defect is masked by xfail or skip, ratchet keys are content-anchored, fixtures delegate to the production seam, and test data is production-shaped.
+steps:
+- title: Assert the observable contract
+  description: |
+    Assert the observable contract (returned value, HTTP status and body, persisted event or JSONL, on-disk state, rendered output) — not the internal call graph or which collaborator was invoked.
+- title: Pin desired behaviour instead of masking defects
+  description: |
+    Do not mask a defect with xfail or skip keyed on "not implemented" / "not blocked" / "current implementation"; pin the desired behavior as a strict, red-first acceptance assertion instead.
+- title: Anchor ratchet keys on stable content
+  description: |
+    Anchor ratchet and allow-list keys on stable content (symbol qualname plus normalized token line, or an AST node), never on file.py:NNN line numbers that drift on benign edits.
+- title: Build fixtures through the production seam
+  description: |
+    Build test fixtures by delegating to the production seam (a single schema authority), not a parallel hand-rolled copy that silently rots when the schema changes.
+- title: Use production-shaped test data
+  description: |
+    Use production-shaped test data (real identifier formats and lengths); do not embed handcrafted placeholders that mask real behavior.
diff --git a/packs/built-in/procedures/op-or-mission-lifecycle.procedure.yaml b/packs/built-in/procedures/op-or-mission-lifecycle.procedure.yaml
