@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: read-intent-before-high-risk-operation
+title: Read Intent Before a High-Risk Operation
+description: |
+  Before a high-risk git or file operation, read the mission spec and current context, escalate when intent is unclear, and never delete a test to make a build pass without confirmed intent.
+entry_condition: |
+  A high-risk operation (merge, rebase, branch or file deletion, force operation, or deleting a test) is about to be executed.
+exit_condition: |
+  The operation proceeded only after the mission spec and context were read and its intent was clear, or it was escalated to the operator.
+steps:
+- title: Read the spec and context first
+  description: |
+    Before executing any high-risk git operation (merge, rebase, deletion of branches or files, force operations), read the mission spec and the current context first. Never execute from a task title or a one-line description alone.
+- title: Escalate unclear intent
+  description: |
+    If the intent of a high-risk operation is unclear or the context is insufficient, escalate to the operator rather than proceeding. Correctness takes precedence over speed.
+- title: Never delete a test to make a build pass
+  description: |
+    Never delete a test to make a build pass; such a deletion is a high-risk operation that requires explicit intent confirmation.
diff --git a/packs/built-in/procedures/readable-pr-preparation.procedure.yaml b/packs/built-in/procedures/readable-pr-preparation.procedure.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..67b7e8f
--- /dev/null
