@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: readable-pr-preparation
+title: Readable Pull Request Preparation
+description: |
+  Prepare a mission branch as a readable draft pull request: rebase and compact it, finish small remaining scope, obtain an independent aggregate review, write a self-contained PR body, and verify the compacted tree before force-pushing.
+entry_condition: |
+  A mission branch is ready to be proposed as a draft pull request.
+exit_condition: |
+  The branch is rebased ahead-only and compacted into readable slices, remaining scope is finished or tracked, an aggregate review verdict is folded in, the PR body carries the evidence, and the compacted tree was verified and re-tested before the force-push with lease.
+steps:
+- title: Rebase and compact the branch
+  description: |
+    Rebase the mission branch onto the current upstream mainline so it is ahead-only, and compact it into a small set of readable, logically-sliced commits (for example docs / surface / repoints) per the clean-linear-commit-history tactic (a non-reordering, behaviour-preserving snapshot chain) — never an interactive reorder. Prefer rebase over merge for integrating the upstream base.
+- title: Confirm the intended scope is complete
+  description: |
+    Before opening the draft PR, confirm the intended scope is complete. If a remaining item is small enough to finish now, finish it; only defer work that is genuinely high-effort or mission-sized, and when deferring, record it as a tracked follow-up with a one-line rationale.
+- title: Obtain an independent aggregate review
+  description: |
+    Obtain an independent review of the aggregate diff before or in parallel to opening the draft PR — the adversarial review squad (adversarial-squad-deployment) is the recommended mechanism. Synthesize a LAND / HOLD verdict and fold every real finding in while the PR is still a draft. Per-WP green and green CI are not, by themselves, the final gate.
+- title: Write a self-contained PR body
+  description: |
+    Write a PR body that states the change, the review evidence (per-WP plus the aggregate squad verdict), and any remaining reviewer or Sonar work, so a later reviewer does not re-derive the context.
+- title: Verify the compacted tree before force-pushing
+  description: |
+    Verify the compacted, rebased tree is identical to the pre-compaction tree except for intentionally-dropped ignored artefacts, and re-run the affected tests on the rebased tip before force-pushing with lease.
diff --git a/packs/built-in/procedures/red-first-bug-reproduction.procedure.yaml b/packs/built-in/procedures/red-first-bug-reproduction.procedure.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..470be42
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packs/built-in/procedures/red-first-bug-reproduction.procedure.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: red-first-bug-reproduction
+title: Red-First Bug Reproduction
+description: |
+  Capture a bug with a reproduction test that fails because the bug manifests, through the entry point that exists on the unfixed code, prove it red before fixing, and confirm the fix with a live run before calling the bug resolved.
+entry_condition: |
+  A bug is to be fixed.
+exit_condition: |
+  A reproduction test, driven through the pre-existing entry point, was shown to fail for the right reason on the unfixed code and passes after the fix, and a live reproduction run has confirmed the corrected behaviour.
+steps:
+- title: Write the reproduction test first
+  description: |
+    When fixing a bug, write a reproduction test first that fails, then apply the fix.
+- title: Reproduce through the pre-existing entry point
+  description: |
+    Reproduce the bug through the PRE-EXISTING (stable) entry point — the command, public function, or seam that exists on the unfixed code — never through the fix's not-yet-written API. A reproduction test must go red BECAUSE THE BUG MANIFESTS in the assertion (the wrong value/status/path/state), not because a new symbol or parameter the fix introduces is missing (ImportError/TypeError at collection).
+- title: Prove red-first, then green
+  description: |
+    Prove red-first — run the reproduction test against the unfixed code and confirm it fails for the right reason, then apply the fix and confirm green. New-API unit tests are fine as contract coverage, but they are not the bug-capture.
+- title: Confirm the fix with a live run
+  description: |
+    After committing a fix, do not consider the bug resolved until a live run confirms the corrected behavior is present. A code inspection that "looks fixed" is not evidence — carry the defect OPEN until a live reproduction run produces the expected (fixed) output. For the red-first pre-existing-entry-point discipline (bugfix test must fail against pre-fix code through the stable entry point, not through the fix's new API), see DIRECTIVE_034.
diff --git a/packs/built-in/procedures/red-main-handling.procedure.yaml b/packs/built-in/procedures/red-main-handling.procedure.yaml
