+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: term-interpretation-alignment
+title: Term Interpretation Alignment
+description: |
+  Before acting on a task, surface its domain-specific and ambiguous terms, state the interpretation in use, have the requester settle real ambiguity, and record the confirmed reading.
+entry_condition: |
+  A task description has been received and work on it has not yet started.
+exit_condition: |
+  Every domain-specific or ambiguous term has a stated interpretation, ambiguous terms have been resolved by the requester, and the confirmed interpretation is recorded in the task artefact or an ADR.
+steps:
+- title: Scan the task for ambiguous terms
+  description: |
+    Scan the task description for domain-specific terms, terms with multiple valid interpretations, and ambiguous references ("the service", "the model", "that component").
+- title: State the interpretation in use
+  description: |
+    For each identified term, state the interpretation being used, including which bounded context it applies to and any assumptions made.
+- title: Ask the requester to resolve ambiguity
+  description: |
+    Where a term has multiple plausible meanings, surface the alternatives and ask the requester to choose before proceeding.
+- title: Record the confirmed interpretation
+  description: |
+    Record the confirmed interpretation in the task artefact or ADR so that future agents inheriting the work share the same understanding.
