+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: tidy-first-campsite-clean
+title: Tidy-First Campsite Clean
+description: |
+  Before implementing a functional change, campsite-clean the surfaces it will modify in a distinct, behaviour-preserving step, so that the functional change that follows is smaller, safer, and easier to review.
+entry_condition: |
+  A mission or work package is about to modify a surface whose clutter (Sonar findings, over-long functions, files, or classes, duplicated call hierarchies) would make the functional change riskier or harder to review.
+exit_condition: |
+  The opening cleanup has landed as its own behaviour-preserving step with focused tests, scoped to surfaces the mission will touch, and the functional change can proceed on the tidied surface.
+steps:
+- title: Campsite-clean the surface before the functional change
+  description: |
+    Tidy-first / enabler sequencing: at the start of a mission or work package that will modify a given surface, campsite-clean that surface FIRST — resolve its Sonar findings, extract or decompose over-long functions/files/classes, and refactor the methods about to change — before implementing the functional change, whenever doing so de-risks or simplifies it. Uncluttering a surface up front makes the subsequent change smaller, safer, and easier to review; a god-module or duplicated call hierarchy fights every edit. The opening cleanup is behavior-preserving, scoped to surfaces the mission will touch, carries focused tests, and is kept as a distinct step preceding the functional change. On heavily-touched god-surfaces, dispatch a campsite scout at planning to census complexity, pull the file's Sonar findings, and list SAFE (WP-opening) / ADJACENT (boy-scout) / OUT (file as a separate issue) cleanups.
+- title: Keep the tidy-first step outside the change-scope resolution order
+  description: |
+    Tidy-first carve-out: an opening campsite-clean performed under Boy Scout Rule's tidy-first / enabler sequencing is a distinct, behavior-preserving step that PRECEDES THE FUNCTIONAL CHANGE, and may legitimately open its own surfaces for that purpose. The change-scope resolution order of RECONCILE_CHANGE_SCOPE_TENSIONS governs the functional change that follows, not this preparatory step.
