+schema_version: '1.0'
+id: targeted-mission-test-run
+title: Targeted Mission Test Run
+description: |
+  Validate mission work with targeted test runs: name the exact test files and gates for the change, never sweep heavy suites, bound parallelism, record the commands run, leave out-of-radius reds to CI, and widen only on the operator's explicit request.
+entry_condition: |
+  Mission work needs local test validation, or a dispatch brief or WP prompt asks an implementer or reviewer to validate a change.
+exit_condition: |
+  Only the targeted test surface (named gate files, mirrored test files, the module's fast tier) ran with bounded parallelism, the exact commands and pass/fail counts are recorded in the PR, and out-of-radius reds were classified rather than chased.
+steps:
+- title: Identify the targeted test surface
+  description: |
+    Identify the targeted test surface before running anything — the test file(s) mirroring each source module the diff touches, the SPECIFIC architectural gate file(s) that guard the change (name them — e.g. `tests/architectural/test_layer_rules.py` for an import-direction change, `tests/architectural/test_no_dead_symbols.py` for a dead-symbol change — never the bare directory), and the owning module's fast tier (`make test-fast` plus the module's own test directory).
+- title: Never run heavy suites whole
+  description: |
+    Never invoke `pytest tests/architectural/` (or any other heavy suite directory) as a whole during mission work; invoke only the named gate file(s) relevant to the change. Never invoke `tests/e2e/`, a full `tests/integration/` sweep, `-m performance`, `-m stress`, `-m timing`, or `make test-full` during mission work for the same reason.
+- title: Name specific gates in briefs and prompts
+  description: |
+    When writing a dispatch brief or a WP prompt that asks an implementer or reviewer to validate a change, name the specific gate files and targeted directories in the prompt's validation section; do not write an instruction that reads as "run the full architectural/e2e/performance suite" or that would resolve to one.
+- title: Bound parallel test runs
+  description: |
+    When lanes run in parallel on one machine, bound `pytest-xdist` explicitly (e.g. `-n 4`); never `-n auto` on a shared machine, and never launch a second concurrent run of the same suite (see `no-parallel-duplicate-test-runs`).
+- title: Record the exact commands run
+  description: |
+    Record the exact targeted commands run and their pass/fail counts in the PR's Tests run section, per the standing test policy.
+- title: Leave out-of-radius reds to CI
+  description: |
+    Treat a red result outside the change's blast radius as CI's to report, not yours to chase locally — classify it via the baseline-red gotcha (pre-existing known-P0 red, CI-environment failure, stale install, or stale venv) instead of running a broader local sweep to investigate it.
+- title: Widen only on explicit operator request
+  description: |
+    Exception: only run a full heavy-suite sweep locally during mission work when the operator explicitly asks for it by name (e.g. "run the full architectural suite" or "run test-full"); an agent's own judgment that a change is risky is not sufficient grounds to widen the run — escalate the risk assessment to the operator instead.
